  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 135 PM CST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will transition to steep southwest flow by early \nWednesday. The pressure gradient and mixed layer winds will be the \ngreatest on Wednesday. Wind gusts of 30 to 40 mph remain possible \nWednesday afternoon. The peak gust potential and boundary layer \nmixing efficiency may be limited by cloud cover over the northwest. \nA strong short wave will be arriving within this flow late Wednesday \ninto Wednesday night. The potential for showers and storms with this \nsystem continue to hinge on the amount of moisture return. The \ncurrent focus is on the the 800-650 mb layer. Should this layer \nsaturate enough, lapse rates above this layer are sufficient for \nfree ascent and could realize convective instability. \n\nSouthwest flow aloft will remain in the wake of the short wave \npassage as a closed upper low will move into the western CONUS. This \nsystem will translate quickly east and arrive Friday into Saturday. \nInitial precipitation chances Friday will be associated with the \ntheta-e advection wind ahead of the primary system followed by the \nmain system Friday night into Saturday. Highs in the 50s and 60s \nwill be common prior to this system followed by cooler weather.",
